# 09 JIT stack control: pcre2_jit_stack_create()
# https://www.pcre.org/current/doc/html/pcre2jit.html
#
# Not exposed by PHP. The JIT stack is hardcoded in PHP. When a match exhausts it PHP reports
# PREG_JIT_STACKLIMIT_ERROR and userland has nothing to adjust.
#
# What it is: JIT-compiled matching runs on its own stack and PCRE2 lets
# the caller create that stack at any size and share it between patterns.
# The jitstack subject modifier below sets the stack size in KiB for one
# match call.
#
# What it enables: patterns that really do need deep recursion keep JIT
# speed instead of hitting an unavoidable stack limit. The other direction
# works too... a deliberately small stack as a resource cap.

# Expect: Failed: error -46: JIT stack limit reached
# 500 levels of recursion do not fit a 1 KiB JIT stack.
/^(a(?1)?a)$/jit
    \=jitstack=1

# Expect: 0: (the whole 500-character subject), 1: (the same)
# The identical call with a 512 KiB stack completes the match.
/^(a(?1)?a)$/jit
    \=jitstack=512
